WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
You know the feeling you get
when you learn something new

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.180
about a health problem
you’ve been trying to reverse?

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.660
Maybe high blood pressure,
diabetes, or heart disease.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.320
Well, there’s nothing I like better
than bringing you the information

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.080
that will help you do just that.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.600
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.480
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.500
Today we deal with pain:
chronic, debilitating pain.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.620
And we look at how anti-
inflammatory diets can be effective

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.261
in alleviating chronic
pain syndromes.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.140
Fibromyalgia is a common disorder

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.220
whose cardinal manifestation
is chronic, widespread pain.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.840
Well, not so common, affecting
2 to 4% of the population

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.680
though probably more like
2%, and especially women.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.540
For decades, some medical
professionals dismissed fibromyalgia

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.500
as all in people’s heads, but this
outdated view has been refuted

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.320
by more recent research
characterizing it as a disorder

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.360
of pain regulation and sensitization.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.500
Brain imaging studies have shown
several perturbations of pain

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.200
processing and regulation
that amplify pain

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.340
in people with the condition.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.780
Twin studies have shown that about
half of fibromyalgia is genetic,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.000
but the other half we
can do something about.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.880
There are lots of drugs with
lots of side effects to help

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.880
with some of the symptoms, but
what about lifestyle approaches?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.600
Engagement in regular
physical activity is considered

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.740
imperative for effective
management of ﬁbromyalgia.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.200
A systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.060
of randomized clinical
trials on the

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.820
effectiveness of therapeutic
exercise in fibromyalgia

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.000
found that both aerobic
and resistance exercises

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.340
are effective ways of reducing pain

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.240
and improving global well-being
in people with fibromyalgia.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.520
Patients may worry and
perceive that exercise

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.560
will worsen their pain and fatigue,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.500
and so you have to start slow and
work your way up as tolerated,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.220
with the goal of eventually
achieving 30 to 60 minutes

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.420
of moderate intensity aerobic
exercise in addition to

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.160
muscle strengthening exercises
(1 to 3 sets of 8–11 exercises,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.000
8–10 repetitions with
a load of about 7 pounds

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.700
or 45% of the max you can lift.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.460
But what about dietary
interventions in terms of

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.680
dialing down the pain sensitivity?

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.600
Well, what causes it in the
first place? Inflammation.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.560
During the inﬂammatory response,
pain receptors are activated,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.100
and chronic inflammation,
can cause chronic activation,

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.520
which may cause chronic
pain, due to this prolonged

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.340
hypersensitization
of pain pathways.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.360
No wonder, then, that
a pro-inﬂammatory diet

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.880
was found to be associated
with pain hypersensitivity

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.280
in patients with
fibromyalgia syndrome.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.120
Exactly which foods
are pro-inflammatory

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.428
and which foods
are anti-inflammatory?

00:02:50.428 --> 00:02:52.080
Check out those twin videos,
but broadly speaking

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.720
components of processed
foods and animal products,

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.120
such as saturated fat,
trans fat, and cholesterol,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.980
were found to be
pro-inflammatory,

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.800
while constituents
of whole plant foods,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.180
such as fiber and phytonutrients,
were strongly anti-inflammatory.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.420
The intake of dietary fiber,
found concentrated in

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.400
only one place—
whole plant foods—

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.000
is fundamental to reducing not
only the risk of abdominal pain

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.620
but also muscle and joint pain,

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.500
we think because of these
short chain fatty acids

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.500
that our good gut bugs
produce when we eat fiber.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.800
These short chain fatty acids
are important mediators of pain,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.040
fundamentally because
they modulate inﬂammation.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.700
So having a lot of fiber-feeding
bugs in your colon is like

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.580
carrying around your own anti-
inflammatory compound factory.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.160
But to cultivate them you actually

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.260
have to eat the
foods that feed them.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:45.300
And in terms of phytonutrients,
plant-derived polyphenols

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.420
are widely acknowledged to also
act as anti-inﬂammatory substances.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.840
Here’s some foods packed with
anti-pain pathway nutrients:

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.780
berries, greens, citrus, nuts,

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.260
spices like turmeric and ginger,
edamame, and green tea.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.620
That’s why you can do randomized,
double-blind crossover trials

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.140
showing that about three cups
worth of strawberries a day

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.020
can significantly improve
pain and inflammation.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.600
If that’s what a
single plant can do,

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.720
what about a diet chock
full of plant foods?

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.300
Put people on a strictly
plant-based diet rich in

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.880
fresh fruits and vegetables, whole
grains and various legumes,

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.040
which are beans, split peas,
chickpeas, and lentils,

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.620
as well as nuts and
seeds, and you can drop

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.460
C-reactive protein
levels 33% in 3 weeks,

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:29.580
which is a leading blood marker
of systemic inflammation.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.120
But does that translate
into less pain?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.740
And the answer is yes, when it
comes to migraine headaches.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.080
Yes when it comes
to painful periods.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.920
A signiﬁcant reduction in menstrual
pain, duration of pain, intensity

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.720
in addition to
premenstrual symptoms.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.780
In fact even just a
single plant, cinnamon,

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.420
about a third of a teaspoon three
times a day during your period

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.780
can help, though it doesn’t
work as well as ibuprofen.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.820
Ginger powder,
on the other hand—

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.320
ground ginger – has been found

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.960
to be comparable to
ibuprofen in relieving pain

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.417
in women with painful cramps.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.800
Whole-food plant-based
diets also alleviate

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.600
the symptoms of osteoarthritis.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.900
Several studies have shown
improvements in rheumatoid arthritis

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.060
symptoms with diets
excluding animal products,

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.640
though it may be just
as much a function of

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.800
increasing the quantity
of healthy plant foods.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.680
But it’s not just because plant-
based diets are so effective

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.200
in causing weight loss,
even at the same weight

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.540
there’s an improvement
in rheumatoid arthritis

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.460
from more plant-based diets.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.720
And plant-based diets can also
alleviate fibromyalgia symptoms.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.840
This is the latest study,
which enrolled anyone

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.080
with chronic musculoskeletal
pain, fibromyalgia or not.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:41.040
Yes, diets high in animal proteins
and fats have been linked to

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.680
chronic pain and inﬂammation,
while plant-based diets

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.540
produce anti-inﬂammatory responses.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.900
So, did it actually work when
put to the test for pain?

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.980
Yes.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.800
Consumption of a
plant-based diet produced

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.840
positive improvements
in chronic pain and function.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:55.800
How much?

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:59.280
Well, a minimally clinically
important diﬀerence in

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.580
chronic musculoskeletal
pain is 1 point on the

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.640
Numeric Pain Rating Scale,
which is just a scale of 1 to 10,

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.320
on how much pain you’re feeling.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.000
And on the plant-based diet

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.340
perceived pain
decreased an average of

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.080
three points on
a 10-point scale,

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.140
from an average of 5 or
6 out of 10 down to 2.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.100
Now, unlike most of prior studies
there was no control group,

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.400
but what’s the downside of
giving healthier eating a try?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.460
In fact, those with chronic pain
are more likely to be overweight

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.300
and have nutrition-related maladies
such as high blood pressure,

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.540
diabetes, and heart disease
all of which can be prevented,

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.060
arrested, and in some
cases even reversed

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.740
with a healthy-enough
plant-based diet.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.760
So, any pain benefit is just
icing on the cake of health.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.980
Uh...scratch that.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:44.700
How about...

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:49.376
the dollop of guacamole
on your bean burrito.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.000
In our next story,

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.187
we look at how apple peels can
help those with chronic joint pain.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.780
Regular apple intake is associated

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:01.320
with all sorts of good
things, like living longer,

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.600
particularly a lower risk
of dying from cancer.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.780
Here’s the survival
curve of elderly women

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.460
who don’t eat an apple a day.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.100
Ten years out,
nearly a quarter died,

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.920
and 15 years out,
nearly half were gone.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.320
But, those who average like

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.260
a half an apple a day
didn’t drop off as fast,

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.820
and those eating an apple a day—

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.080
more than 3 and a half ounces—

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.520
like a cup of apple slices,

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.920
stayed around even longer.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.320
Yeah, but maybe people who eat apples

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.640
every day just happen to practice

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.020
other healthy behaviors

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.360
like exercising more, or not smoking,

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.940
and that’s really why they’re living longer.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.760
Well, they controlled for most of that–

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.340
obesity, smoking status,
poverty, diseases, exercise—

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:45.720
so as to compare apples
to apples (so to speak).

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.480
But, what they didn’t control for

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.580
was an otherwise healthier diet.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:53.220
Studies show that those who regularly

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.020
eat apples have higher intakes

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.080
of not just nutrients like
fiber, found in the apples,

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.240
but they’re eating less added sugar,

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.460
less saturated fat—in other words,

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.500
they’re eating overall healthier diets;

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.860
and so, no wonder
apple eaters live longer.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.920
But is apple eating just
a marker for healthy eating,

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:11.700
or is there something about

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.680
the apples themselves that’s beneficial?

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.960
You don’t know, until...

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.940
you put it to the test.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.509
There are all sorts of fun studies

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:22.260
like this, where subjects were randomly

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.340
assigned in the morning to nothing,

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:27.300
a caffeinated energy drink,
black coffee, or an apple,

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.580
given that athletes use a variety

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.080
of common strategies to stimulate

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.000
arousal, cognition, and performance

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.740
before their morning training.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.380
Did the apple hold its weight?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:40.260
Yes, appearing to work just as well

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.580
as the caffeinated beverages.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.340
The problem with these
kinds of studies though,

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.720
is they’re not blinded.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.340
Those in the apple group knew

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.600
they were eating an apple,

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.780
and so, there may have been
this expectation bias,

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:54.480
placebo effect, that
made them unconsciously

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.400
give that extra bit of
effort in the testing

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.360
and skew the results.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:00.600
You just can’t stuff a
whole apple into a pill.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.300
That’s why researchers, instead,

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.360
test specific extracted apple components;

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.420
so, they can perform a double-blind
placebo controlled study,

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:10.980
where half get the fruit elements,

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.000
half get the sugar pill,

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.520
and you don’t know until
the end who got which.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.340
The problem there, though, is that

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.260
you’re no longer dealing
with a whole food,

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.720
removing the symphony of interactions

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.460
between the thousands of phytonutrients

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:24.720
in the whole apple.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.580
Most of these special nutrients

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.040
are concentrated in the peel, though.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.380
Instead of just dumping millions

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.060
of pounds of nutrition in the trash,

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.600
why couldn’t researchers
just dry and powder the peels

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.000
into opaque capsules to disguise them

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.280
and then run blinded studies with that?

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.980
Even just a small amount could greatly

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.420
increase phytochemical content

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.340
and antioxidant activity.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.340
The meat industry got the memo:

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.680
dried apple peel powder decreases microbial

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.600
expansion in meat and protects against

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:57.120
carcinogen production when you cook it.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.820
And, one of the carcinogens formed

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.020
during the grilling of meat

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:04.140
is a beta carboline alkaloid, a neurotoxin,

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.820
which may be contributing to the

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:08.100
development of neurological diseases,

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.206
like Parkinson’s.

00:10:09.206 --> 00:10:11.280
I did a video about it awhile ago.
Uncooked meat doesn’t have any;

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:14.640
the neurotoxin is formed
when you cook it,

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.340
but you can cut the levels in half

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.880
by first marinating the meat
with dried apple peel powder.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.620
And also cuts down on the amount of

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.921
fecal contamination bacteria in the meat.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.880
Apple peels can also inhibit the formation

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.660
of genotoxic, DNA-damaging,
heterocyclic amines,

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.120
cutting the levels of these
cooked meat carcinogens

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.620
by up to more than half.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.800
In view of the risks
associated with consuming

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.140
these cancer causing
compounds in meat,

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.540
there is a need to reduce exposure

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:45.240
by blocking HCA formation,

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.100
such as by adding apple powder

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.720
during the cooking of meats

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:49.980
to help prevent their production.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.180
I mean, I can’t think of any other
way to reduce exposure. (mocking)

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.880
What about consuming apple peels directly?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.440
Dried apple peel powder was found

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.860
to exhibit powerful anti-inflammatory
and antioxidant action,

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.560
but this was in mice.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.680
Does it have anti-inflammatory
properties in people?

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.060
You don’t know...

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.220
until you put it to the test.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:14.280
A dozen folks with moderate loss of joint

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.200
range of motion and
associated chronic pain

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:19.560
were given a spoonful
of dried apple peels

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:21.600
a day for 12 weeks,

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:24.600
and pain scores dropped
month after month,

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.460
and the range of motion improved

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.740
in their neck, shoulders, back, and hips.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.460
Conclusion: consumption of
dried apple peel powder

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.660
was associated with improved

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.160
joint function and pain reduction.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.920
Why just “associated”?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.620
Because there was no control group;

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.240
so, they might have all been

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.680
just getting better on their own,

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.180
or it could have been a placebo effect.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:49.440
But hey, why not give apple peels a try,

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:54.071
by eating more apples.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.660
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.060
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.880
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:06.300
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:09.840
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.720
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.000
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.480
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:22.020
My last two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:24.180
and the “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.180
Stay tuned for December 5, 2023

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.840
for the launch of my new one,
How Not to Age.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.080
And, of course, all the proceeds
I receive from the sales

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.480
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.980
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.660
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.840
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:48.180
Everything on the
website is free.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.520
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorship,

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.030
no kickbacks.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:53.460
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.000
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.220
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:03.667
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

